% The E12 convention in a legal-readable view: an external value the
% contract reads (a price feed) is an ASSUMABLE template. With the price
% stated (by whom: the trailer says) the view answers outright; without it,
% it answers conditionally, naming the price it would need — the question a
% borrower actually asks. A live feed would be the same template with
% `; via service feed` and a declared service (docs/le_summary.md §17.6):
% the answer is then attributed to the service and cached, and can be
% materialised as a plain fact — no syntax of its own either way.
%
% How the files relate. vault.le is the translated twin (borrow left as
% residue), vault_oracle.le the twin with borrow filled in (the price as a
% fluent the feed's event sets): this view states the same borrow condition
% as vault_oracle.le's constraint, written by hand as a timeless rule (the
% generated legal view of vault.le — the editors' Legal View command — covers
% only what vault.le translates: deposit). A view is a Prolog-target program and an LPS twin is
% not, so neither includes the other.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the price of the collateral is at least *a number*; assumable.
    the collateral of *an account* is *an amount*; undefined.
    the debt of *an account* is *an amount*; undefined.
    *a caller* may borrow *an amount*.

the knowledge base vault view includes:

% Vault.sol, borrow: reverts Undercollateralised when collateral * price < 2 * (debt + amount)
a caller may borrow an amount A if
    the collateral of the caller is an amount C
    and the debt of the caller is an amount D
    and C > 0
    and a number P = 2 * (D + A) / C
    and the price of the collateral is at least P.

scenario unknown_price is:
    the collateral of alice is 100.
    the debt of alice is 0.
    borrow expects answers ["alice may borrow 90"] and unknowns ["the price of the collateral is at least 1.8"].

scenario known_price is:
    the collateral of alice is 100.
    the debt of alice is 0.
    the price of the collateral is at least 1.8, according to the price feed.
    borrow expects answers ["alice may borrow 90"].

query borrow is:
    alice may borrow 90.
